{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "lurescan",
          "version": "0.1.0",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "LS-SUP-001",
              "name": "EditorTaskRunsAutomaticallyWhenTheFolderIsOpened",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Editor task runs automatically when the folder is opened"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "VS Code and compatible editors run tasks with runOptions.runOn=folderOpen as soon as the workspace opens, once automatic tasks are allowed. Fake job repositories use this to run a payload when the candidate opens the project."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Do not allow automatic tasks for untrusted folders. Remove the task, keep the folder in Restricted Mode, and treat any machine that already ran it as compromised.\n\nFramework alignment:\n- OWASP-Web A08 Software and Data Integrity Failures\n- CSA-CCM STA-08 Supply Chain Risk Management\n- CSA-CCM TVM-02 Malware Protection Policy and Procedures\n- CSA-CCM UEM-09 Anti-Malware Detection and Prevention\n- ATT&CK T1195.001 Supply Chain Compromise: Compromise Software Dependencies and Development Tools\n- ATT&CK T1204.002 User Execution: Malicious File\n- ATT&CK T1059 Command and Scripting Interpreter\n- CWE CWE-506 Embedded Malicious Code\n- CWE CWE-829 Inclusion of Functionality from Untrusted Control Sphere\n- NIST-SSDF PO.5 Implement and Maintain Secure Environments for Software Development\n- NIST-SSDF PW.4 Reuse Existing, Well-Secured Software When Feasible"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "supply-chain",
                  "OWASP-Web:A08",
                  "CSA-CCM:STA-08",
                  "CSA-CCM:TVM-02",
                  "CSA-CCM:UEM-09",
                  "ATT&CK:T1195.001",
                  "ATT&CK:T1204.002",
                  "ATT&CK:T1059",
                  "CWE:CWE-506",
                  "CWE:CWE-829",
                  "NIST-SSDF:PO.5",
                  "NIST-SSDF:PW.4"
                ],
                "precision": "high",
                "security-severity": "8.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "LS-SUP-002",
              "name": "RemoteContentPipedIntoAShellInterpreter",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Remote content piped into a shell interpreter"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A command downloads content and executes it immediately (curl|sh, iwr|iex, mshta URL, certutil download). Nothing on disk records what ran."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Remove the command. Never execute downloaded scripts without pinning and reviewing them.\n\nFramework alignment:\n- OWASP-Web A08 Software and Data Integrity Failures\n- CSA-CCM TVM-02 Malware Protection Policy and Procedures\n- CSA-CCM UEM-09 Anti-Malware Detection and Prevention\n- ATT&CK T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n- ATT&CK T1059.004 Command and Scripting Interpreter: Unix Shell\n- ATT&CK T1059.003 Command and Scripting Interpreter: Windows Command Shell\n- CWE CWE-494 Download of Code Without Integrity Check\n- CWE CWE-829 Inclusion of Functionality from Untrusted Control Sphere\n- NIST-SSDF PW.4 Reuse Existing, Well-Secured Software When Feasible\n- NIST-SSDF PS.2 Provide a Mechanism for Verifying Software Release Integrity"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "malware",
                  "OWASP-Web:A08",
                  "CSA-CCM:TVM-02",
                  "CSA-CCM:UEM-09",
                  "ATT&CK:T1105",
                  "ATT&CK:T1059.004",
                  "ATT&CK:T1059.003",
                  "CWE:CWE-494",
                  "CWE:CWE-829",
                  "NIST-SSDF:PW.4",
                  "NIST-SSDF:PS.2"
                ],
                "precision": "high",
                "security-severity": "9.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "LS-SUP-003",
              "name": "NpmLifecycleScriptExecutesCodeDuringInstall",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "npm lifecycle script executes code during install"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "preinstall, install, postinstall and prepare run automatically on npm install. Background launches (nohup, start /b) or downloads in these hooks are a hallmark of fake job repositories."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Install untrusted projects with --ignore-scripts inside a disposable VM, and remove the hook.\n\nFramework alignment:\n- OWASP-Web A08 Software and Data Integrity Failures\n- CSA-CCM STA-08 Supply Chain Risk Management\n- CSA-CCM TVM-02 Malware Protection Policy and Procedures\n- ATT&CK T1546.016 Event Triggered Execution: Installer Packages\n- ATT&CK T1195.002 Supply Chain Compromise: Compromise Software Supply Chain\n- ATT&CK T1059.007 Command and Scripting Interpreter: JavaScript\n- ATT&CK T1564.003 Hide Artifacts: Hidden Window\n- CWE CWE-506 Embedded Malicious Code\n- CWE CWE-829 Inclusion of Functionality from Untrusted Control Sphere\n- NIST-SSDF PW.4 Reuse Existing, Well-Secured Software When Feasible\n- NIST-SSDF PS.1 Protect All Forms of Code from Unauthorized Access and Tampering"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "supply-chain",
                  "OWASP-Web:A08",
                  "CSA-CCM:STA-08",
                  "CSA-CCM:TVM-02",
                  "ATT&CK:T1546.016",
                  "ATT&CK:T1195.002",
                  "ATT&CK:T1059.007",
                  "ATT&CK:T1564.003",
                  "CWE:CWE-506",
                  "CWE:CWE-829",
                  "NIST-SSDF:PW.4",
                  "NIST-SSDF:PS.1"
                ],
                "precision": "high",
                "security-severity": "8.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "LS-CON-001",
              "name": "CodeHiddenAfterALongRunOfWhitespace",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Code hidden after a long run of whitespace"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A line continues with code after 80 or more spaces, pushing it off-screen in editors without word wrap."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Inspect the full line with word wrap on. Hidden trailing code is a strong malware indicator.\n\nFramework alignment:\n- CSA-CCM TVM-02 Malware Protection Policy and Procedures\n- ATT&CK T1564 Hide Artifacts\n- ATT&CK T1027 Obfuscated Files or Information\n- CWE CWE-506 Embedded Malicious Code\n- CWE CWE-912 Hidden Functionality\n- NIST-SSDF PW.7 Review and/or Analyze Human-Readable Code to Identify Vulnerabilities"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "concealment",
                  "CSA-CCM:TVM-02",
                  "ATT&CK:T1564",
                  "ATT&CK:T1027",
                  "CWE:CWE-506",
                  "CWE:CWE-912",
                  "NIST-SSDF:PW.7"
                ],
                "precision": "high",
                "security-severity": "8.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "LS-APP-005",
              "name": "TlsCertificateValidationDisabled",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "TLS certificate validation disabled"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Certificate or revocation checks are turned off, allowing interception or tampering of downloads."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Keep validation on and fix the certificate chain instead.\n\nFramework alignment:\n- OWASP-Web A02 Cryptographic Failures\n- OWASP-Web A08 Software and Data Integrity Failures\n- CSA-CCM CEK-03 Data Encryption\n- CWE CWE-295 Improper Certificate Validation\n- NIST-SSDF PW.9 Configure Software to Have Secure Settings by Default"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "app-security",
                  "OWASP-Web:A02",
                  "OWASP-Web:A08",
                  "CSA-CCM:CEK-03",
                  "CWE:CWE-295",
                  "NIST-SSDF:PW.9"
                ],
                "precision": "medium",
                "security-severity": "8.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "LS-LURE-002",
              "name": "ReadmeInstructsACommandThatTriggersHiddenExecution",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "README instructs a command that triggers hidden execution"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The setup steps lead the reader to run install or start commands that set off the hooks or tasks found elsewhere in the repository."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Do not follow the instructions. Inspect in a disposable VM with scripts disabled.\n\nFramework alignment:\n- CSA-CCM HRS-11 Security Awareness Training\n- CSA-CCM TVM-02 Malware Protection Policy and Procedures\n- ATT&CK T1566.003 Phishing: Spearphishing via Service\n- ATT&CK T1204.002 User Execution: Malicious File\n- CWE CWE-506 Embedded Malicious Code\n- NIST-SSDF PO.5 Implement and Maintain Secure Environments for Software Development"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "lure",
                  "CSA-CCM:HRS-11",
                  "CSA-CCM:TVM-02",
                  "ATT&CK:T1566.003",
                  "ATT&CK:T1204.002",
                  "CWE:CWE-506",
                  "NIST-SSDF:PO.5"
                ],
                "precision": "high",
                "security-severity": "8.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "LS-APP-001",
              "name": "AuthenticationResultHardCodedToSuccess",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Authentication result hard-coded to success"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A password or authentication check is set to true, so any credentials are accepted."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Compare against the stored hash with bcrypt.compare or equivalent, and fail closed.\n\nFramework alignment:\n- OWASP-Web A07 Identification and Authentication Failures\n- CSA-CCM IAM-14 Strong Authentication\n- CSA-CCM IAM-16 Authorization Mechanisms\n- ATT&CK T1190 Exploit Public-Facing Application\n- CWE CWE-287 Improper Authentication\n- NIST-SSDF PW.5 Create Source Code by Adhering to Secure Coding Practices\n- NIST-SSDF PW.7 Review and/or Analyze Human-Readable Code to Identify Vulnerabilities"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "app-security",
                  "OWASP-Web:A07",
                  "CSA-CCM:IAM-14",
                  "CSA-CCM:IAM-16",
                  "ATT&CK:T1190",
                  "CWE:CWE-287",
                  "NIST-SSDF:PW.5",
                  "NIST-SSDF:PW.7"
                ],
                "precision": "high",
                "security-severity": "8.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "LS-CON-003",
              "name": "RuntimeApiReachedThroughComputedNames",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Runtime API reached through computed names"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Globals such as Function or Buffer are resolved from character codes or concatenated strings, or a function is called with a 'require' parameter. This hides an eval-style call from text search."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Decode the expression statically and review what it executes before running anything.\n\nFramework alignment:\n- CSA-CCM TVM-02 Malware Protection Policy and Procedures\n- CSA-CCM UEM-09 Anti-Malware Detection and Prevention\n- ATT&CK T1027 Obfuscated Files or Information\n- ATT&CK T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n- ATT&CK T1059.007 Command and Scripting Interpreter: JavaScript\n- CWE CWE-506 Embedded Malicious Code\n- CWE CWE-95 Eval Injection\n- NIST-SSDF PW.7 Review and/or Analyze Human-Readable Code to Identify Vulnerabilities"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "concealment",
                  "CSA-CCM:TVM-02",
                  "CSA-CCM:UEM-09",
                  "ATT&CK:T1027",
                  "ATT&CK:T1140",
                  "ATT&CK:T1059.007",
                  "CWE:CWE-506",
                  "CWE:CWE-95",
                  "NIST-SSDF:PW.7"
                ],
                "precision": "high",
                "security-severity": "8.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "LS-CON-005",
              "name": "LargeEncodedBlobEmbeddedInSource",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Large encoded blob embedded in source"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A long, high-entropy hex, base64, or byte-array literal usually carries an encrypted or packed payload."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Decode the blob offline and inspect it as untrusted data. Never pass it to eval or Function.\n\nFramework alignment:\n- CSA-CCM TVM-02 Malware Protection Policy and Procedures\n- ATT&CK T1027.013 Obfuscated Files or Information: Encrypted/Encoded File\n- ATT&CK T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n- CWE CWE-506 Embedded Malicious Code\n- NIST-SSDF PW.7 Review and/or Analyze Human-Readable Code to Identify Vulnerabilities"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "concealment",
                  "CSA-CCM:TVM-02",
                  "ATT&CK:T1027.013",
                  "ATT&CK:T1140",
                  "CWE:CWE-506",
                  "NIST-SSDF:PW.7"
                ],
                "precision": "medium",
                "security-severity": "8.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "LS-LURE-001",
              "name": "ReadmeAdvertisesBlockchainComponentsThatAreAbsent",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "README advertises blockchain components that are absent"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The README describes contracts, NFTs, or DeFi features, but no contract sources or toolchain are present. Fake job repositories wrap a repurposed app in an invented Web3 story."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Verify the company and the project through independent channels before running anything.\n\nFramework alignment:\n- CSA-CCM HRS-11 Security Awareness Training\n- ATT&CK T1566.003 Phishing: Spearphishing via Service\n- ATT&CK T1036 Masquerading\n- NIST-SSDF PO.5 Implement and Maintain Secure Environments for Software Development"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
